    "q-89855": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89855",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}?$\n\nI. The range of $f(x)$ is $(-10,\\infty )$\n\nII. $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\nIII. The graph of $f(x)$ lies in the second and fourth quadrants",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt[3]{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14216358/assets/abafb7d55b4baa0b06f20c3de2b44d5925f7286f078aaa76d71aded7c9c9a001.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $f(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\n- Statement III is false since the graph of $f(x)$ lies in the first and third quadrants\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
